\appendix

\section{Changes from our earlier version}
\label{app:v1}

A first version of this dataset, submitted as a course deliverable on 8 November 2026, used a single risk label.
In it, every L3 negative (a poisoned record with a neutral query) was the same input as an L1 positive with the
opposite label, for 878 training and 359 test inputs. It also had one trigger in training and one held out, so
the L3 test could only be passed by memorising a string. Numbers from that version are not comparable to those
here and should not be cited. The two outputs, the per-record triggers and the wrong-trigger and overlap negatives
were introduced to fix these problems. The earlier results are kept in the repository under \texttt{results/v1/}.

